<title>POLAND: REMAK WINS PLN 6.4 MLN CONTRACT.</title>
<headline>REMAK WINS PLN 6.4 MLN CONTRACT.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish engineering company Remak SA won a 6.4-million-zloty contract for the modernisation of waste storage containers at the Polish Turow power station in central Poland, the company said in a statement on Thursday.</p>
<p>Work on the project will be carried out from November 1996 to May 1997, the statement said.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
